From b17b0f419a4b30bc8c72e885a07f37fa052b1a63 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 07:19:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): an owner-wake supervisor card may unblock the
 cards its body lists [daveey]

On 10-28..10-30 four hub cards sat in triage 1.5-3 days. chat-closeout's owner
wake routes an orphaned owner's cards to a board-supervisor card, but its worker
could only comment: kanban_unblock is orchestrator-only and the only worker grant
was the self-heal fix card's.

requeue_grant() generalizes self_heal_requeue_grant: the self-heal grant is
unchanged, and a card created_by='owner-wake' whose title starts 'Owner wake:
supervise' may unblock exactly the <board>/<id> card lines of its body that
resolve to this board, only while the target is in triage or blocked. Such a
worker gets the kanban_unblock tool (has_requeue_grant). Audit event
owner_wake_requeue. Every other worker and target stays refused (t_01a18ba39f9cb81a).
